class:: DoubleWellProcess
summary:: Metastable diffusion in a nonlinear potential
categories:: UGens>Generators>Stochastic>Processes
related:: Guides/Stochastica, Classes/OUProcess, Classes/RandomTelegraph, Classes/BrownNoise

description::

DoubleWellProcess wanders inside an energy landscape with two preferred regions. It can remain near one well for a long time before noise pushes it over the barrier. This metastability makes slowly changing timbres and competing generative states, while retaining continuous fluctuation within each region. link::Classes/OUProcess:: has one preferred mean; this process commonly has two.

The equation is code::dx = (a*x-b*x^3+drive)dt + abs(noise)dW::, with potential code::V(x) = b*x^4/4-a*x^2/2-drive*x::. Positive a and b with zero drive give stable wells at plus/minus code::sqrt(a/b)::. Negative a or b are allowed and may leave the double-well regime or diverge. The model follows the standard overdamped bistable system used in stochastic-resonance research; see R. Benzi, Stochastic Resonance: from climate to biology (2007), link::https://arxiv.org/abs/nlin/0702008::, and Gammaitoni et al. (1998), link::https://doi.org/10.1103/RevModPhys.70.223::.

Fixed Euler-Maruyama substeps hold the current inputs throughout each calculation. Each adds the deterministic drift times dtSub and a normal innovation scaled by code::abs(noise)*sqrt(dtSub)::. Small time steps are essential for stiff or strongly driven systems; increasing substeps improves numerical accuracy at a proportional CPU cost. There is no hidden clipping, folding, or binary classification. If a state becomes non-finite or cannot be represented as a server float, the whole calculation recovers to current initial without reseeding. Non-finite scalar inputs become zero.

Reset starts in the chosen well, not in a stationary distribution. Settling and rare barrier crossings can take time. The examples accelerate model time so the behavior is apparent within seconds. A weak periodic tilt can become more effective at causing transitions with moderate noise; adding still more noise need not improve drive-related switching.

Like link::Classes/BrownNoise:: it can drive wandering modulation, but its nonlinear restoring force creates preferred wells and its raw state is not bounded to an audio range.

