classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: drive
Additive force tilting the potential; default 0. Audio-rate input is allowed.
argument:: a
Linear drift coefficient; default 1. Not forced positive.
argument:: b
Cubic restoring coefficient; default 1. Not forced positive.
argument:: noise
Diffusion magnitude per square-root model second; default 0.35. Uses absolute value.
argument:: timeScale
Model seconds per real second; default 1. Nonpositive holds state.
argument:: initial
State at construction/reset and numerical recovery; default -1.
argument:: substeps
Init-rate integer clipped to 1..16; default 1.
argument:: seed
Init-rate local PCG32 seed. Zero derives a seed from the parent Synth; nonzero is reproducible. Reset restores the original seed.
argument:: reset
Rising edge restores current initial and the original seed. No integration on that calculation.
returns:: One raw, unnormalized process state.

method:: kr
Control-rate version: one calculation spans the full control block. Event outputs last one block.

instancemethods::

examples::

subsection:: A metastable trajectory

Watch fluctuations and occasional crossings.

code::
(
{ DoubleWellProcess.kr(noise: 0.7, timeScale: 8, substeps: 4).poll(10) }.play
)
::

subsection:: Metastable timbre

The continuously changing state moves between two spectral regions without throwing away within-well motion.

code::
(
{
    var state = DoubleWellProcess.kr(noise: 0.75, timeScale: 6, substeps: 4);
    Pan2.ar(RLPF.ar(Saw.ar(90, 0.06), state.tanh.linexp(-1, 1, 180, 4500), 0.2))
        * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.05)
}.play
)
::

subsection:: Weak drive and stochastic resonance

Left has no noise; right has moderate noise. The same subthreshold drive tilts both wells. Listen over several periods; this is a qualitative example, not a universally optimal noise setting.

code::
(
{
    var drive = SinOsc.kr(0.2) * 0.25;
    var states = DoubleWellProcess.kr(drive, noise: [0, 0.65], timeScale: 8, substeps: 8, seed: 37);
    SinOsc.ar(states.tanh.linexp(-1, 1, 180, 850), 0, 0.06) * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.05)
}.play
)
::
